# package-contract checks — in-scope paths only: packages/mpd-tui-plugin/, evidence/tui/plugin/

## 1. no cordis.patch.yml inside the package (the bundle patch owns the row)
$ find packages/mpd-tui-plugin -name 'cordis.patch.yml'
(empty output above means: no patch file)
$ grep -rn 'insert:' packages/mpd-tui-plugin
(no patch row written by this package)

## 2. no dsh.bundle key in the package manifest (this task introduces no loader entry id)
$ node -e "const m=require('./packages/mpd-tui-plugin/package.json'); console.log('dsh field present:', 'dsh' in m)"
dsh field present: false

## 3. relative imports in src/ (only the vendored schemastery PACKAGE DIRECTORY is extensionless)
$ grep -rn 'from "\.\./' packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src | grep -v '\.js"'
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/index.ts:34:import z from "../../mpd-agent-teams-plugin/_deps/schemastery"
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/settings.ts:17:import z from "../../mpd-agent-teams-plugin/_deps/schemastery"

## 4. no stdout writes in src (TUI frame discipline)
$ grep -rn 'console\.|require(|process\.stdout' packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/log.ts:4:// is live — a plugin that console.log()s corrupts the rendered frame. Every

## 5. theme asset is valid JSON with the required base key
$ node -e "const t=require('./packages/mpd-tui-plugin/themes/mpd-tui.json'); console.log(t.name, t.base, Object.keys(t.colors).length+' colors')"
mpd-tui dark 11 colors

## 6. packaged skill frontmatter (single-line scalars only)
$ head -4 packages/mpd-tui-plugin/skills/mpd-tui/SKILL.md
---
name: mpd-tui
description: Use when a user in a DSH-TUI session asks for the mpd board, the mpd status line, or the workmate library — and when explaining which mpd capabilities are TUI-native and which are still web-only.
---

